---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Layout title="Integrations — Fathom" description="Configure Fathom workers with CRM, MCP, optional browser and LSP services, notifications, search backends, and export formats.">
  <main class="integrations-page">
        <PageHero cls="int-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="intPage.hero.badge">Integrations</p>
        <h1 class="h2-sec" data-i18n-html data-i18n="intPage.hero.title">Connect to <em class="it">your stack.</em></h1>
        <p class="copy-lg mx-auto" data-i18n="intPage.hero.sub">Configure CRM, MCP, optional browser and LSP services, notifications, search backends, and export formats for self-hosted autonomous work.</p>
    </PageHero>
    <div class="container">

      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="intPage.categories.badge">Integration Categories</p>
        <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="intPage.categories.title">Connectors for one worker runtime</h2>
        <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n="intPage.categories.sub">Choose the connectors your deployment needs. Configure credentials and endpoints; workers discover available tools while governance controls side effects.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="api-grid api-grid--2col">
        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">📊</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.crm.name">CRM Sync</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.crm.desc">Configured amoCRM (API v4), Bitrix24 (REST API), and HubSpot (CRM v3) connectors let workers sync contacts and findings. Deduplication by crm_id and retry behavior depend on the connector configuration.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">amoCRM</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Bitrix24</span>
            <span class="api-tag">HubSpot</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">🔌</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.mcp_client.name">MCP Client</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.mcp_client.desc">stdio and HTTP transports support dynamic tool discovery and reconnect handling. Configured external tools become available to workers subject to policy; define them with the supported `name`, `transport`, `command`, `args`, and `url` fields.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">stdio</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Streamable HTTP</span>
            <span class="api-tag">HTTP / stdio</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">📡</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.mcp_server.name">MCP Server</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.mcp_server.desc">mcp-serve exposes the runtime's available tools over Model Context Protocol and executes real tool calls. Optional browser tools appear when a CDP endpoint is reachable, and computer tools appear when COMPUTER_URL is configured; MCP clients can drive the toolbox permitted by policy.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">tools vary by configuration</span>
            <span class="api-tag">tools/list</span>
            <span class="api-tag">tools/call</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">🖥️</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.browser.name">Browser Automation</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.browser.desc">When an operator supplies a reachable Chrome DevTools Protocol endpoint, workers can use navigate, screenshot, click, type, and extract against that browser, including JS-heavy pages and authenticated sessions.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">CDP</span>
            <span class="api-tag">navigate</span>
            <span class="api-tag">screenshot</span>
            <span class="api-tag">click</span>
            <span class="api-tag">type</span>
            <span class="api-tag">extract</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">📣</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.notifications.name">Notifications</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.notifications.desc">Configured webhook (JSON POST), email (SMTP via lettre), or Telegram Bot API channels can receive run events. Fan-out and per-channel error isolation are runtime behaviors to verify in your deployment.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">Webhook</span>
            <span class="api-tag">SMTP</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Telegram</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">🔍</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.lsp.name">LSP Integration</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.lsp.desc">With a configured language-server command, workers can use document_symbols, goto_definition, find_references, hover, and workspace_symbols through LSP. Installation and supported languages remain operator-managed.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">symbols</span>
            <span class="api-tag">definitions</span>
            <span class="api-tag">references</span>
            <span class="api-tag">hover</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">🔎</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.search.name">Search Backends</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.search.desc">Configured search backends can include Linkup, Parallel.ai, Exa, Tavily, Serper, Brave, or DuckDuckGo. Select a default in config or per query where supported; custom implementations can use the SearchBackend trait.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">Linkup</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Exa</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Tavily</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Serper</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Brave</span>
            <span class="api-tag">Parallel.ai</span>
            <span class="api-tag">DuckDuckGo</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="api-card api-card--wide">
          <div class="api-icon">📦</div>
          <div class="api-name" data-i18n="intPage.categories.export.name">Export Formats</div>
          <p data-i18n="intPage.categories.export.desc">Workers can export structured results as CSV (RFC 4180), vCard 3.0, JSON, XLSX, PDF, HTML, or DOCX where the corresponding exporter is enabled — contacts, findings, and reports included.</p>
          <div class="api-tags">
            <span class="api-tag">CSV</span>
            <span class="api-tag">vCard</span>
            <span class="api-tag">JSON</span>
            <span class="api-tag">XLSX</span>
            <span class="api-tag">PDF</span>
            <span class="api-tag">HTML</span>
            <span class="api-tag">DOCX</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feat feat-reverse">
        <div class="feat-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="intPage.config.badge">Configuration</p>
          <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="intPage.config.title">Configure the runtime you operate</h2>
          <p class="copy-lg" data-i18n="intPage.config.sub">The self-hosted runtime reads integration settings from ~/.fathom/config.toml where supported. Define CRM credentials, MCP servers, notification channels, and search defaults; some services also require their own endpoint or process.</p>
          <div class="more-links">
            <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-primary" data-i18n="intPage.config.docs">Full documentation</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-card">
          <pre><code># ~/.fathom/config.toml

[crm]
provider = "hubspot"          # hubspot | amocrm | bitrix24
domain = "mycompany.hubspot.com"
api_key = "pat-xxx"

[[mcp.servers]]
name = "postgres"
transport = "stdio"
command = "npx"
args = ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres"]

[[mcp.servers]]
name = "internal-api"
transport = "http"
url = "https://mcp.internal.corp"
# HTTP transport uses the configured URL

[notifications]
webhook_url = "https://hooks.slack.com/..."
telegram_bot_token = "..."
email_smtp = "smtp://mail.corp:587"

[search]
default_backend = "tavily"
tavily_api_key = "..."</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="int-cta">
        <h2 class="h3-sec" data-i18n="intPage.cta.title">Connect deliberately, then run</h2>
        <p class="copy-lg mx-auto" data-i18n="intPage.cta.sub">Configure only the credentials and services your workers need, start the runtime, and let governed tool calls sync contacts, notify channels, or export results under your operator policy.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-primary" data-i18n="intPage.cta.docs">Read the docs</a>
          <a href="/tools" class="btn btn-secondary" data-i18n="intPage.cta.tools">Browse tools</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .integrations-page { padding: 70px 0 90px; }

  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .16px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--grey-600); }
  .h2-sec { font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 68px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.02; }
  .h3-sec { font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 12px 0 16px; }
  .copy-lg { color: var(--grey-700); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 640px; }
  .mx-auto { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  .int-hero {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto 56px;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .int-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .int-hero .copy-lg { margin-top: 20px; }

  .sec-head {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 36px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .api-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 2px; background: var(--grey-300); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--grey-300); margin-top: 30px; }
  .api-card { background: var(--bg-card); padding: 26px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; transition: background var(--duration) var(--ease-out); }
  .api-card:hover { background: var(--bg-secondary); }
  .api-card .api-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
  .api-card p { color: var(--grey-600); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .api-icon { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .api-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .api-grid--2col {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .api-card--wide {
    padding: 28px 28px;
  }

  .api-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .api-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--grey-700);
    background: var(--grey-100);
    border: 1px solid var(--grey-200);
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    transition: all var(--duration) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .api-tag:hover {
    border-color: var(--grey-400);
    color: var(--grey-900);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) { .api-grid--2col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .feat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; padding: 64px 0; }
  .feat-reverse { direction: rtl; }
  .feat-reverse > * { direction: ltr; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .feat, .feat-reverse { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; direction: ltr; } }

  .code-card { border: 1px solid var(--grey-200); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-dark); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); }
  .code-card pre { margin: 0; padding: 22px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-card code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--grey-100); white-space: pre; }

  .more-links { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 24px; }

  .int-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 64px 0 24px;
  }

  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 32px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
</style>
